<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1942</h1><p class="ref-lede">1942 in world history: 41 events, 15 births, 15 deaths, 2 works, 3 states founded and 1 that came to an end. 712 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1938">1938</a><a href="/years/1939">1939</a><a href="/years/1940">1940</a><a href="/years/1941">1941</a><a href="/years/1942" aria-current="page">1942</a><a href="/years/1943">1943</a><a href="/years/1944">1944</a><a href="/years/1945">1945</a><a href="/years/1946">1946</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-1">1 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Twenty-six Allied nations sign the Declaration by United Nations</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Meeting in Washington, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and others pledged to fight the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> together and make no separate peace. The term '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a>' later named the post-war organisation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/manila" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manila.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-2">2 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Japanese forces occupy Manila</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a>, declared an open city after American and Filipino forces withdrew to Bataan. The Philippine capital remained under Japanese occupation until its devastating liberation in 1945.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-13">13 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Henry Ford patents a plastic car body</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry Ford received a patent for a car body built from plastic panels on a tubular frame, part of his experiments with materials derived from soybeans. Wartime restrictions ended the project.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-20">20 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nazi officials meet at Wannsee to coordinate the Holocaust</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Chaired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reinhard-heydrich">Reinhard Heydrich</a>, senior officials met at a villa on the Wannsee in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> to organise the 'Final Solution', the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportation</a> and murder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a>. The minutes survived the war.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-15">15 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Singapore surrenders to Japan</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">General Arthur Percival surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a>, and some 80,000 British, Indian and Australian troops became prisoners. Churchill called it the worst disaster and largest capitulation in British history.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/singapore">Singapore</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-19">19 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Roosevelt signs Executive Order 9066</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The order allowed the military to exclude people from designated areas, leading to the internment of about 120,000 Japanese Americans. Congress apologised and paid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-reparations">reparations</a> in 1988.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-8">8 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Japanese forces occupy Rangoon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Japanese troops entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>'s capital, abandoned by the British. The loss cut the Burma Road supply route to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, and by May <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> controlled most of Burma.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-14">14 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Penicillin saves its first American patient</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Anne Miller, dying of streptococcal blood poisoning after a miscarriage, was treated at a New Haven hospital with a scarce supply of penicillin. She recovered and lived to the age of 90.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-12">12 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Red Army opens its offensive at Kharkov</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces attacked around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kharkiv">Kharkov</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> to regain the initiative. German forces encircled the attackers within days, and the disaster cost the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> more than 200,000 men.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-3">3 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Midway opens with US air attacks</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Bombers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway">Midway</a> Atoll attacked the approaching Japanese invasion force. The next day US carrier aircraft sank four Japanese carriers, turning the tide of the Pacific war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway">Battle of Midway</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-4">4 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US dive-bombers wreck Japan's carrier force at Midway</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Within minutes American dive-bombers set three Japanese carriers ablaze; a fourth was hit that afternoon. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> lost its best carriers and many experienced aircrew.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-7">7 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Battle of Midway ends with the sinking of Yorktown</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The damaged carrier USS Yorktown finally sank as the battle closed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s loss of four <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aircraft-carrier">fleet carriers</a> ended its naval superiority in the Pacific.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-midway">Battle of Midway</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/vel-dhiv-roundup" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vel-dhiv-roundup.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/july-17">17 July</a> · Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/vel-dhiv-roundup">Vel' d'Hiv Roundup</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Vel' d'Hiv Roundup was a mass arrest of Jews in Paris on 16–17 July 1942, carried out by French police under the Vichy government at German request.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/solomon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/solomon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-7">7 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US Marines land on Guadalcanal</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">US Marines landed on Guadalcanal in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> Islands, the first major American offensive of the Pacific war. Six months of fighting ended in a Japanese withdrawal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/ethiopian-empire">Ethiopian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-19">19 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Red Army launches Operation Uranus at Stalingrad</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces attacked the weak Romanian-held flanks north and south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volgograd">Stalingrad</a>. Within four days they encircled the German Sixth Army, which surrendered in February 1943.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-26">26 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Casablanca premieres in New York</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casablanca">Casablanca</a>, starring Humphrey Bogart and Ingrid Bergman, premiered at the Hollywood <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a> weeks after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> landed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. It won three Academy Awards, including Best Picture.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">Theatre</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-2">2 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Fermi's team achieves the first controlled nuclear chain reaction</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Under the stands of Stagg Field at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-chicago">University of Chicago</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enrico-fermi">Enrico Fermi</a>'s team started a self-sustaining chain reaction in Chicago Pile-1. It opened the way to atomic bombs and nuclear power.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-java-sea" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-java-sea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-java-sea">Battle of the Java Sea</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of the Java Sea was a naval battle fought on 27 February 1942 during the Second World War, in which a Japanese fleet defeated an Allied squadron of Dutch, British, Australian and American ships.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/fall-of-singapore" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fall-of-singapore.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/fall-of-singapore">Fall of Singapore</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The fall of Singapore was the surrender of the British garrison to Japanese forces in February 1942, after a rapid campaign through Malaya.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/second-battle-of-el-alamein" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-battle-of-el-alamein.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/second-battle-of-el-alamein">Second Battle of El Alamein</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Second Battle of El Alamein was fought in Egypt in 1942 between British Commonwealth forces under Bernard Montgomery and the German-Italian army under Erwin Rommel.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/rio-protocol" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rio-protocol.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/rio-protocol">Rio Protocol</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Rio de Janeiro Protocol was signed on 29 January 1942 by Ecuador and Peru after Peru's victory in the war of 1941, with Argentina, Brazil, Chile and the United States as guarantors.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/operation-torch">Operation Torch</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Operation Torch was the Allied invasion of French North Africa in November 1942, with landings around Casablanca, Oran and Algiers.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/wannsee-conference" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wannsee-conference.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/wannsee-conference">Wannsee Conference</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Wannsee Conference was a meeting of senior Nazi officials held at a villa on the Wannsee lake in Berlin on 20 January 1942.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bataan">Battle of Bataan</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Bataan was fought from January to April 1942 on the Bataan Peninsula of Luzon, where American and Filipino forces under Douglas MacArthur withdrew after the Japanese invasion of the Philippines.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bir-hakeim" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-bir-hakeim.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bir-hakeim">Battle of Bir Hakeim</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Bir Hakeim was fought in the Libyan desert from 26 May to 11 June 1942, as part of the Battle of Gazala.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-madagascar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-madagascar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-madagascar">Battle of Madagascar</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Madagascar was the Allied campaign of 1942 to take Vichy French Madagascar and deny its harbours to Japan.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/kokoda-track-campaign" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kokoda-track-campaign.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Campaign</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/kokoda-track-campaign">Kokoda Track campaign</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Kokoda Track campaign was fought between July and November 1942 in the Owen Stanley Range of Papua, then an Australian territory.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/quit-india-movement">Quit India Movement</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Quit India Movement was a mass campaign launched by the Indian National Congress on 8 August 1942, demanding an immediate end to British rule.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/sook-ching" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sook-ching.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/sook-ching">Sook Ching</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Sook Ching, meaning &quot;purge through cleansing&quot;, was the mass killing of ethnic Chinese by the Japanese military in Singapore and Malaya after the fall of Singapore in February 1942.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-corregidor-1942">Battle of Corregidor (1942)</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Corregidor was the last stand of American and Filipino forces in the Philippines in 1942, on the fortified island at the mouth of Manila Bay.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/cripps-mission">Cripps Mission</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Cripps Mission was a British attempt in March and April 1942 to secure Indian cooperation in the Second World War.</p></div></li></ol></section>
